# REQUIRES: cuda, python-api
# The products of force matching with virtual sites
# (D[force-matching-sites], #771 part 2), on a GPU:
# - linear sites (OPC of GROMACS): the product in theta of D381 and the
#   derivative in the positions of D383 against central differences of a
#   NumPy Phi and of Phi from the evaluator, and mixed against double;
# - the extra points of Amber (OPC from a prmtop, cut by ParmEd): the
#   product in theta against a NumPy Phi, the derivative in the positions
#   refused by name;
# - on rigid waters, the two placements are one place (the same energy).
# Inputs/python_frame_sites.py says what each scenario checks.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_sites.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide pair GPU Double %t/pair-Double | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=PAIR,DOUBLE -DMODE="GPU Double"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_sites.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide pair GPU Mixed %t/pair-Mixed | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=PAIR,MIXED -DMODE="GPU Mixed"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_sites.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide box GPU Double %t/box-Double | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=BOX,DOUBLE -DMODE="GPU Double"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_sites.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide box GPU Mixed %t/box-Mixed | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=BOX,MIXED -DMODE="GPU Mixed"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_sites.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide amber GPU Double %t/amber-Double | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=AMBER,AMBERDOUBLE -DMODE="GPU Double"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_sites.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide amber GPU Mixed %t/amber-Mixed | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=AMBER,AMBERMIXED -DMODE="GPU Mixed"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_sites.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide placement GPU Double %t/placement-Double | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=PLACEMENT -DMODE="GPU Double"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_sites.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide placement GPU Mixed %t/placement-Mixed | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=PLACEMENT -DMODE="GPU Mixed"

# PAIR: [[MODE]]: two OPC waters: the NumPy energy against the evaluator
# PAIR: [[MODE]]: two OPC waters: the NumPy gradient (zero on the sites) against the evaluator
# PAIR: [[MODE]]: two OPC waters, 2 frames of 8 particles: the product in theta against central differences of the NumPy Phi
# PAIR: [[MODE]]: two OPC waters: the product in theta of the variant against D381's
# PAIR: [[MODE]]: two OPC waters: the derivative in the positions against central differences of the NumPy Phi
# BOX: [[MODE]]: eight OPC waters in 2.0 nm: the NumPy energy against the evaluator
# BOX: [[MODE]]: eight OPC waters in 2.0 nm, 2 frames of 32 particles: the product in theta against central differences of the NumPy Phi
# BOX: [[MODE]]: eight OPC waters in 2.0 nm: the product in theta of the variant against D381's
# BOX: [[MODE]]: eight OPC waters in 2.0 nm: the derivative in the positions against central differences of the NumPy Phi
# DOUBLE: [[MODE]]: {{.*}}: the same against central differences of Phi from the evaluator
# MIXED: [[MODE]]: {{.*}}: the product in theta in mixed precision against that in double
# MIXED: [[MODE]]: {{.*}}: the derivative in the positions in mixed precision against that in double
# PAIR: [[MODE]]: two OPC waters: the derivative in the positions with another cotangent on the sites
# BOX: [[MODE]]: eight OPC waters in 2.0 nm: the derivative in the positions with another cotangent on the sites
# AMBER: [[MODE]]: Amber OPC (ACE-ALA-NME and 40 waters, 182 particles), 2 frames: the product in theta against central differences of the NumPy Phi
# AMBERDOUBLE: [[MODE]]: Amber OPC (ACE-ALA-NME and 40 waters, 182 particles): the same against central differences of the rows along the cotangent
# AMBERMIXED: [[MODE]]: Amber OPC (ACE-ALA-NME and 40 waters, 182 particles): the product in theta in mixed precision against that in double
# AMBER: Amber OPC: the derivative in the positions is refused by name; the product in theta stays, to the bit
# PLACEMENT: [[MODE]]: OPC from Amber and from GROMACS (40 waters, a = {{[0-9.]+}}), 2 frames of rigid waters: the energy, through the places of the sites
